 "fn-1": "<a href=\"https://1073shoso.jp/www/sankyo/detail.jsp?id=18666\"><code>kashima-kainyo-1987</code></a> - 「According to a survey carried out in Showa 62 (1987) at Kashima, Tonami city (46 households), of a total of 1,542 trees of 10 centimeters or more in diameter, sugi numbered 735, making up 48 percent, about half of the whole, an average of 16 per household.」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「昭和６２年の砺波市鹿島（世帯数４６戸）での調査によると、直径１０センチ以上の全樹木数１，５４２本の内、スギは７３５本で全体の約半数の４８パーセントを占め、１戸当たり平均１６本であった。」)",
 "fn-2": "<a href=\"https://1073shoso.jp/www/sankyo/detail.jsp?id=18666\"><code>kashima-kainyo-1987</code></a> - 「According to a survey at Kashima, Tonami city (46 households) in Showa 62 (1987)」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「昭和６２年の砺波市鹿島（世帯数４６戸）での調査によると」)",
 "fn-3": "<a href=\"https://visit-toyama-japan.com/en/travel-inspiration/sankyoson\"><code>visit-toyama-sankyoson</code></a> - \"A dispersed settlement with over 7,000 houses (farmhouses) surrounded by homestead woodlands extends in the area of approx. 220 km2.\" / \"Kainyo has protected houses and people's lives from cold seasonal winds and snowstorms in winter and sunlight in summer.\" (the source's own English)",
 "fn-4": "<a href=\"https://1073shoso.jp/www/sankyo/detail.jsp?id=18666\"><code>kashima-kainyo-1987</code></a> - 「Of a total of 1,542 trees of 10 centimeters or more in diameter, sugi numbered 735, making up 48 percent, about half of the whole, and averaged 16 per household.」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「直径１０センチ以上の全樹木数１，５４２本の内、スギは７３５本で全体の約半数の４８パーセントを占め、１戸当たり平均１６本であった。」)",
 "fn-5": "<a href=\"https://1073shoso.jp/www/sankyo/detail.jsp?id=18666\"><code>kashima-kainyo-1987</code></a> - 「The remaining roughly 50 percent were 83 species, beginning with matsu (pine) and kaki (persimmon).」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「残りの約５割はマツやカキをはじめとする８３種であった。」)",
 "fn-6": "<a href=\"https://1073shoso.jp/www/sankyo/detail.jsp?id=18666\"><code>kashima-kainyo-1987</code></a> - 「The number of tree species per household runs from 1 species to 14 species, averaging about 6 species.」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「１戸平均樹種数は１種から１４種で平均６種程度である。」)",
 "fn-7": "no publicly readable source (searched 2026-09-12: the Tonami archive page carrying the 1987 Kashima survey was fetched with its Shift_JIS charset honored and read in full - it gives 1,542 trunks over 46 households, 735 of them cedar, 83 other species and 1 to 14 species a household, and no homestead of 200 trees or 31 species; the Tonami Kainyo Club's own explainer page carries no tree counts at all, and a ministry landscape case study none either; the figure reaches the record from a search summary, which is a pointer and never a source)",
 "fn-8": "<a href=\"https://1073shoso.jp/www/sankyo/detail.jsp?id=18666\"><code>kashima-kainyo-1987</code></a> - 「Also, within the homestead grounds there is always a bamboo stand, and it has fulfilled the role of a utility species.」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「また屋敷内には必ずタケ林があって実用種としての役目を果たしてきた。」) (Also, every homestead has a bamboo stand, which has served as a utility species.) Also on the page: 「Tree heights run from 11 meters to 28 meters, averaging about 15 meters.」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「樹高は１１メートルから２８メートルで平均１５メートルくらいである。」) - tree heights 11-28 m, about 15 m on average.<!-- Extra, not asserted in this section but load-bearing for the belt height below -->",
 "fn-9": "<a href=\"https://1073shoso.jp/www/sankyo/detail.jsp?id=18666\"><code>kashima-kainyo-1987</code></a> - 「Sorting the species of the homestead grove into a tall-tree layer (10 m and over), a medium layer (5-10 m), a shrub layer (1-5 m) and a low-shrub layer (under 1 m): 44, 76, 80 and 153 species respectively - a truly rich flora.」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「屋敷林に入っている樹種を高木層（１０メートル以上）中木層（５〜１０メートル）、低木層（１〜５メートル）、小低木層（１メートル以下）に区分し観察すると、発生している樹種は、高木層４４種、中木層７６種、低木層８０種、小低木層１５３種と実に豊富である。」)",
 "fn-10": "<a href=\"https://1073shoso.jp/www/sankyo/detail.jsp?id=18666\"><code>kashima-kainyo-1987</code></a> - 「The yashikirin as it has been: around the house, from the south face round to the west, tall trees - mainly sugi, with oak and zelkova; from the west face round to the north, hackberry and alder with a little bamboo; on the east, flowering trees, persimmon, fig and the like.」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「今までの屋敷林は、家屋を中心に南面から西面にかけてスギを主体にカシ、ケヤキの高木が配置され、西面から北面にはエノキ、ハンノキに加え若干のタケが入り、東面には花木やカキ、イチジク等が植えられていた。」); <a href=\"https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/屋敷林\"><code>yashikirin-jawiki</code></a> - 「On the west side and the south side, tall and sturdy trees, chiefly sugi, were planted in preparation against wind and snow.」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「西側や南側には風や雪に備えて杉を中心に背の高く丈夫な木が植えられていた。」)",
 "fn-11": "<a href=\"https://auf.isa-arbor.com/content/37/1/19.full\"><code>isa-auf-fukugi-2011</code></a> - \"When the orientation of the remaining trees were averaged, it was found that the greatest number of large Fukugi trees stand to the north of the house, followed by the eastern side, and then southern side.\" / \"monsoonal winds from the north and typhoons from the eastern side are the greatest threat to property.\" (the source's own English)",
 "fn-12": "<a href=\"https://kdas.jp/test2/detail_display.php?t_cd=1&amp;acc_cd=3&amp;aclc_cd=0&amp;chap=6&amp;hp_page=74&amp;bc_cd=1\"><code>kitamoto-mushiro-niwa</code></a> - 「Usually 40 to 60 mats, and among them were houses that exceeded 100. Incidentally, two mushiro come to one tsubo.」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「普通四〇〜六〇枚、中には百枚を越す家もあった。ちなみに、ムシロ二枚が一坪にあたる。」) (40-60 mats usually, over 100 for some; two mats to a tsubo (the tsubo figures are the record's arithmetic on this).)",
 "fn-13": "<a href=\"https://kdas.jp/test2/detail_display.php?t_cd=1&amp;acc_cd=3&amp;aclc_cd=0&amp;chap=6&amp;hp_page=74&amp;bc_cd=1\"><code>kitamoto-mushiro-niwa</code></a> - 「being related to the area under barley cultivation」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「麦の耕作面積と関係していて」) (related to the barley acreage; the clause sits between the two sentences quoted above)<!-- the fetch returned only the paraphrase 「was related to the area under barley cultivation」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「麦の耕作面積と関連していた」) for this clause; the registry's verbatim is the one shown -->",
