 "fn-17": "<a href=\"https://crd.ndl.go.jp/reference/entry/index.php?id=1000296656&amp;page=ref_view\"><code>ndl-kokumori</code></a> - 「Though it differed by region, the yield per tan had more or less settled at: upper paddy (joden) = 1 koku 5 to (a mori of 15), middle paddy (chuden) = 1 koku 3 to (a mori of 13), lower paddy (geden) = 1 koku 1 to (a mori of 11), lowest paddy (gegeden) = 9 to (a mori of 9).」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「地域によって異なるが、１反あたりの収穫量は、上田＝１石５斗（15の盛）、中田＝１石３斗（13の盛）、下田＝１石１斗（11の盛）、下々田＝９斗（９の盛）にほぼ定着していた」)",
 "fn-18": "<a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20230624043456/http://www.knowledgebank.irri.org/grainQuality/module_4/popups/pu_drying.htm\"><code>irri-drying-floor</code></a> - 「For best results, paddy should be spread about 2.5 cm thick over the floor. At this thickness 500 square meters of drying floor can handle 6 tons of paddy.」 <!-- READ 2026-09-06, feature 195; the footnote formerly carried the registry summary -->",
 "fn-19": "<a href=\"https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/aijax/418/0/418_KJ00004075360/_pdf\"><code>kamikanai-1771-houses</code></a> - 「From the Meiwa 8 (1771) 'Account Ledger of the Annual Land Tax on Paddy and Dry Fields' (田畑御年貢算用帳) of Kamikanai village, the holding (mochidaka) of each peasant of Kamikanai village is established.」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「明和8年の上金井村『田畑御年貢算用帳』より，上金井村のそれぞれの百姓の持高が判明する。」)「As for holdings: up to the 4-koku band, 1 house; the 5 to 9 koku band, 13 houses; the 10 to 14 koku band, 15 houses; the 15 to 19 koku band, 2 houses; and over 30 koku, 1 house. Within the 5 to 14 koku band, 28 of the 32 houses fall.」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「持高は，4石台までが1軒，5〜9石台が13軒，10〜14石台が15軒，15〜19石台が2軒，30石余が1軒である。5−14石台の間に32軒中28軒が分布している。」)「The shoya (village headman) is particularly large in both holding and floor area in tsubo」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「庄屋は持高・坪数ともに特に大きく」)「the 20 to 29 tsubo band, 14 houses; the 30 to 39 tsubo band, 5 houses; the 40 to 49 tsubo band, 3 houses」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「20〜29坪台が14軒，30〜39坪台が5軒，40〜49坪台が3軒」) (From the Meiwa 8 (1771) tax ledger each Kamikanai peasant's holding is known; holdings: up to 4 koku 1 house, 5-9 koku 13, 10-14 koku 15, 15-19 koku 2, 30-odd koku 1 - 28 of 32 houses in the 5-14 band; the headman is markedly the largest in both holding and floor area; main houses 20-29 tsubo 14, 30-39 tsubo 5, 40-49 tsubo 3.)<!-- Text is pdftotext output of a scanned layout; the 40-49 bin count is read across a column break. -->",
 "fn-20": "<a href=\"https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/aijsaxx/222/0/222_KJ00003747888/_pdf\"><code>kikoba-kenchi</code></a> - 「Homestead lot areas are distributed between 20 bu and 100 bu」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「屋敷反歩は20歩から100歩の間に分布している」)「with 30 bu and 50 bu showing the peaks」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「30歩と50歩がピークを示し」) (Homestead lot areas are distributed between 20 and 100 bu; 30 bu and 50 bu form the peaks.)",
 "fn-21": "<a href=\"https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/aijax/418/0/418_KJ00004075360/_pdf\"><code>kamikanai-1771-houses</code></a> - 「The scale of Kyoho-period Iwahara main houses ... the relation between holding (mochidaka) and floor area in tsubo is, though there are exceptions, a proportional one in which, if the holding increases by about 5 koku, the floor area increases by about 10 tsubo」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「享保期の岩原主屋規摸は…持高と坪数との関係は，例外もあるが，持高が5石ほど増加すれば坪数が10坪ほど増加するという比例関係」)",
