 "fn-64": "<a href=\"https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/下肥\"><code>shimogoe-jawiki</code></a> - 「For rotting down to ripeness, a container from which the liquid cannot leak is used - such as a jar buried in the ground, or a pit finished with plaster (the koedame).」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「腐熟には、地中に埋めた壺や、漆喰をほどこした穴といった、溶液が漏れることのない容器を用いる（肥溜め）。」)「Fresh night soil is harmful to crops, and when it is to be used as fertilizer it is stored for a fixed period and left to rot to ripeness.」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「新鮮な屎尿は作物にとって有害であり、肥料として用いる際には、一定期間貯蔵して腐熟させる。」) (For ripening, a vessel that does not leak is used - a jar buried in the ground or a plastered pit (the koedame); fresh night soil is harmful to crops and is stored for a period to ripen before use as fertilizer.)",
