 "fn-90": "<a href=\"https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/尺貫法\"><code>shakkanho-jawiki</code></a> - 「1 tsubo (bu) = 10 go = 400/121 square meters, approximately 3.305785 m²」; 「1 se = 30 tsubo (bu), approximately 99.173553 m²」; 「1 tan = 10 se, approximately 991.735537 m²」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「1坪（歩）= 10 合 = 400/121平米 ≒ 3.305785 m²」; original: 「1 畝 = 30坪（歩）≒ 99.173553 m²」; original: 「1反（段）= 10 畝 ≒ 991.735537 m²」)",
 "fn-91": "no publicly readable source (searched 2026-09-12: the Japanese article on the household kitchen garden names the bed but gives no area, and no page was traced that measures a Japanese dooryard bed or a Chinese rice-south farmhouse's dooryard plot)",
 "fn-92": "<a href=\"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E5%9B%9B%E5%90%88%E9%99%A2\"><code>siheyuan-zhwiki</code></a> - 「However, in the North China region the east wing takes the western sun in summer and is struck directly by the cold northwesterly wind in winter, so it is unsuitable for living in; in Shaanxi courtyard houses the east wing is often used by wealthy households to store grain, or as a kitchen or a horse stable.」 (translated from the Chinese by this project; original: 「然而，在中国华北地区，东厢房夏季西晒，冬季直接受到西北冷风吹袭，所以不宜居住，陕西四合院东厢房多被富户用来存储粮物，或作厨房、马厩。」) (an encyclopedia article; the sentence's own reference is a folklore dictionary page that survives only as a 2007 capture, so the citation rests on the article itself and no scholarly survey stands behind it here)",
 "fn-93": "<a href=\"https://www.fao.org/4/s1250e/s1250e11.htm\"><code>fao-farm-structures-cattle</code></a> - 「A shade structure allowing 2.5 to 3m² per animal will give the minimum desirable protection for cattle」 - a modern standard for cattle housing, not a measurement of a premodern byre",
